  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying the least probable (i.e., rarest) favorable outcome in each lottery and comparing their monetary values. However, the individual instead focused on the overall probability of winning (i.e., getting any positive amount), favoring the option with a higher chance of a non-zero outcome. The information considered by the individual (probability of winning) differs from that required by the decision reason (value of the least probable outcome). Furthermore, the justification (maximizing chance of a win) does not align with the rule of the decision reason (maximizing the value of the least likely favorable outcome). Therefore, there is no evidence that the individual used this reason in their decision process.",
